  "result": "I wrote the revised record for `NRS_484B_250_2` to `record.jsonl` in the repair directory. It hasn't been run through the gate yet.\n\n**What failed:** the `blind` scenario hid `rel.bearing` and expected `unknown`. Hiding `rel.bearing` only drops a measured bearing. Core still computes it from the two vehicles' positions and the subject's heading, so the gate decided which vehicle was on the right and returned `violated`.\n\n**Main change:** `blind` now hides `kin.speed` instead. With speed unobserved, the duty can't say whether the subject moved off or stayed at rest, so the verdict is `unknown`. The coder already traced this against the existing rule and blind trace: `kin.speed` comes out as the only unknown reason and everything else stays decided. The blind witness should pass with only its masked id changed. I rewrote the narrative to match. Hiding any other relation Core computes, like `rel.contact` or `rel.centre_distance`, would fail the same way.\n\n**Two tidy-ups, no change in meaning:**\n- I removed the `param_proposals`. All eight parameters are already in the catalogue, so the record names them as they are.\n- I removed the `meaning` from `int.left_turn`, because that id is already in the declared-fact catalogue.\n\nEverything else in the record is unchanged: the span mappings, the applicability and obligation, the parameters and the other six scenarios.",
